<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Ringerike</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 1020 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Inland petty kingdom north-west of Oslo whose last king, Sigurd Syr, was stepfather of Saint Olaf and father of Harald Hardrada.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ringerike lay around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrifjorden">Lake Tyrifjorden</a> in the inland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upplands-norway">Upplands</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>. The sagas name a king Sigurd Hart as ruler here in the 9th century and make his daughter the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a>. Like its neighbours, it was a farming district ruled by local kings who might accept a more powerful overlord.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The area was fertile and well settled, and its kings held large estates. Ringerike lent its name to an art style of the early 11th century, seen on carved stones quarried in the district, with tendrils and animal motifs. Local kings kept their titles under the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair's</a> successors.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Its best-known king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigurd-syr">Sigurd Syr</a>, married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asta-gudbrandsdatter">Åsta</a>, mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Olaf Haraldsson</a>, and supported Olaf's bid for the Norwegian throne in 1015. Sigurd died around 1018, and Olaf soon put an end to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upplands-norway">Uppland</a> petty kings, so Ringerike became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a>. Sigurd's son was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 750 CE – 1020 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:74.63%;width:5.37%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 CE – 1020 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sigurd Syr</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism, later Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Ringerike, Hringaríki</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=885&amp;focus=ringerike" aria-label="Ringerike on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4886 141 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ringerike lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5225 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5206 397h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5206 397h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Norway. <a href="/atlas?year=885&amp;focus=ringerike">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
